    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nComing from coc.nvim there are two little things that I miss and think improve quality of life, allow automatically select the first element so I can just hit tab or enter to select without having to use the arrow keys and automatically adding parentheses after a function is selected from the completion menu and placing the cursor inside. \n\nI looked for a way to configure this but couldn't find one.",
